sentences.l:
but when indeed the swift arrow subdues it,
raw-eating jackals in the mountains tear it
in a shady glen;

“O Nestor, son of Neleus, great glory of the Achaeans,
come, mount your chariot, and beside you Machaon
let him go, and to the ships most quickly drive the solid-hoofed horses;

and they, hearing the stroke,
lightly bore the swift chariot among the Trojans and Achaeans,
treading on the dead and on shields;
